@model vulnerablewebpage.Models.SqlInjectionLabViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "SQL injection";
}
<p><a href="/labs/">← All security exercises</a></p>
<h1>SQL injection: query construction</h1>
<p class="lead">This exercise uses a fresh SQLite <strong>in-memory</strong> database containing four harmless inventory records. The demonstration connection is set to read-only after seeding.</p>

<form method="get" action="/labs/sql-injection" class="card card-body mb-3">
    <label class="form-label" for="term">Product name search</label>
    <input class="form-control mb-3" type="text" id="term" name="term" maxlength="60" value="@Model.Term" />
    <label class="form-label" for="mode">Implementation</label>
    <select class="form-select mb-3" name="mode" id="mode">
        <option value="unsafe" selected="@(!Model.Secure)">Unsafe: concatenate input into SQL</option>
        <option value="safe" selected="@(Model.Secure)">Safer: parameterized query</option>
    </select>
    <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Run query</button>
</form>

<div class="alert @(Model.Secure ? "alert-success" : "alert-danger")" data-testid="sql-outcome">@Model.Outcome</div>
<ul class="list-group mb-3" data-testid="sql-results">
@foreach (var item in Model.Items)
{
    <li class="list-group-item" data-testid="sql-item">@item.Id — @item.Name</li>
}
</ul>
<p>Try the harmless boolean condition <code>' OR 1=1--</code>:
    <a href="/labs/sql-injection?term=%27%20OR%201%3D1--&amp;mode=unsafe">unsafe query</a> ·
    <a href="/labs/sql-injection?term=%27%20OR%201%3D1--&amp;mode=safe">parameterized query</a>.
</p>
<p class="text-muted">For safety this specific exercise rejects statement separators and other characters outside a narrow boolean-injection input set. Its database is recreated per request and is not connected to the main SQL Server database.</p>
